IGAVAC for details.\nL147@P3: 6 Contactor has two coils. Both are used for pick-up, and\nL148@P3: then in approximately 75 milliseconds, one coil is electronically\nL149@P3: removed from the coil drive circuit. The remaining coil supplies\nL150@P3: low continuous hold power sufficient for the contactor to meet\nL151@P3: all of its specified performance specifications. This provides low\nL152@P3: coil power without PWM electronics that can cause EMI emissions\nL153@P3: and/or cross-talk on control power.\nL154@P3: 7 Contactor is operated by a coil that changes resistance\nL155@P3: with temperature. Since Pick-up Current, Coil Current and Coil\nL156@P3: Power are specified at Nominal Voltage, they will be lower than\nL157@P3: indicated at temperatures above 25°C and higher than indicated\nL158@P3: at temperatures below 25°C. Similarly, Pick-up and Drop-out\nL159@P3: Voltages will be higher than indicated at temperatures above\nL160@P3: 25°C and lower than indicated at temperatures below 25°C.\nL161@P3: 8 For pick-up testing of contactors with dual coils, the voltage\nL162@P3: can not be ramped up slowly, but must be applied instantly to at\nL163@P3: least the maximum Pick-up Voltage. Otherwise, the contactor will\nL164@P3: not pick-up.\nL165@P3: 9 Limit make current to 500A to avoid contact welding. For AC\nL166@P3: power switching cycles, contact factory.\nL167@P3: APPLICATION NOTES\nL168@P3: • Contactors feature internal transorb for coil suppression. No external\nL169@P3: diodes should be added across the coil. The use of additional external coil\nL170@P3: suppression can slow the release time and invalidate the life cycle ratings,\nL171@P3: or can cause the contactor not to be able to interrupt the maximum current\nL172@P3: specified. If lower coil back EMF is required, please contact GIGAVAC for\nL173@P3: assistance.\nL174@P3: • Power switching lifecycles are based on current flow from A2(+) to A1(-).\nL175@P3: For best breaking performance, the contactor should be installed so that\nL176@P3: current flows from A2(+) to A1(-). There are cases where the contactor will\nL177@P3: interrupt power in the opposite direction but please contact GIGAVAC to\nL178@P3: confirm suitability. Direction of current flow is not relevant during make\nL179@P3: or when flowing on closed contacts. For bi-directional contactors, please\nL180@P3: contact GIGAVAC.\nL181@P3: • Applications with capacitors will require a pre-charge circuit.\nL182@P3: • Electrical life rating is based on resistive load with 27µH maximum\nL183@P3: inductance in circuit. Because your application may be different, we\nL184@P3: suggest you test the contactor in your circuit to verify life is as required.\nL185@P3: • End of life is defined as when the dielectric, insulation resistance or\nL186@P3: contact resistance fails the specifications listed.\nL187@P3: PART NUMBER SYSTEM\nL188@P3: GX11 B A B\nL189@P3: Coil Voltage B = 12 Vdc, Internal Coil\nL190@P3: Suppression\nL191@P3: C = 24 Vdc, Internal Coil\nL192@P3: Suppression\nL193@P3: F = 48 Vdc, Internal Coil\nL194@P3: Suppression\nL195@P3: H = 72 Vdc, Internal Coil\nL196@P3: Suppression\nL197@P3: J = 120 Vdc, Internal\nL198@P3: Coil Suppression\nL199@P3: K = 120 Vac, Internal\nL200@P3: Coil Suppression\nL201@P3: L = 240 Vac, Internal\nL202@P3: Coil Suppression\nL203@P3: S = 12 Vdc, Low Power,\nL204@P3: Internal Coil Suppression\nL205@P3: T = 24 Vdc, Low Power,\nL206@P3: Internal Coil Suppression\nL207@P3: Coil\nL208@P3: Termination\nL209@P3: A = Flying leads\nL210@P3: 38 cm (15 in)\nL211@P3: B = Flying leads\nL212@P3: 61 cm (24 in)\nL213@P3: C = Flying leads\nL214@P3: 122 cm (48 in)\nL215@P3: Auxiliary\nL216@P3: Contact\nL217@P3: Blank = None\nL218@P3: B = SPST,\nL219@P3: Normally Open\nL220@P3: C = SPST,\nL221@P3: Normally Closed\nL222@P3: GIGAVAC® - 6382 Rose Lane - Carpinteria, CA 93013 - ph +1-805- 684-8401 - fax +1-805- 684-8402\nL223@P3: info@gigavac.com - www.gigavac.com - ©Copyright 2003-2014 GIGAVAC, LLC.\nL224@P